    "    As of 2026, approximately 7.4 million Americans age 65 and older live with clinical Alzheimer’s dementia, which represents about 1 in 9 people in this age group. The incidence increases substantially with age. Approximately 0.4% of adults ages 65–74, 3.2% of adults ages 75–84, and 7.6% of adults age 85 and older develop clinical Alzheimer’s dementia annually. The annual number of new cases is projected to double by 2050 as our older population grows.\n",
